<p class="sounds-lead">Short sounds for a page - a chime when something is saved, a pop, a coin, a
drum - each a tag of its own: a recipe in a file of <code>pad/subs/sounds/types/</code> in the
engine, written <code>{pad:open/}sound:name/{pad:close/}</code>.
No audio file anywhere: the browser makes the sound from its recipe and plays it, and the server
makes the same samples into the WAV file each card links.</p>

<ul class="sounds-board">
  {array:sounds}
    <li class="sounds-card" id="sound-{$kind}">
      <h2 class="sounds-name">{$name}</h2>
      <p class="sounds-line">{$line}</p>
      <div class="sounds-play">{sound:$kind download/}</div>
      <p class="sounds-meta"><code>{pad:open/}sound:{$kind}/{pad:close/}</code> · {$seconds} s · {$voices} {pad:echo $voices eq 1 ? 'voice' : 'voices'/}</p>
      <details class="sounds-recipe">
        <summary>The recipe</summary>
        <pre><code>{!recipe}</code></pre>
      </details>
    </li>
  {/array:sounds}
</ul>
